  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><sup><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/574642/diamond-spheres-erudition-esoterica\">Diamond Spheres: Erudition &amp; Esoterica</a></sup></p>\n<p>Whenever you successfully notice a creature using Stealth, as long as you do not reveal your awareness of the creature’s intent or location, you can take the creature by surprise if they initiate combat within the next minute. If the hostile creatures would normally gain a surprise round against you (and your allies), you act in the surprise round, gain a +4 bonus to the initiative check to determine your place in the surprise round, and you may take both a standard and a move action. If you go first in the initiative count, all hostile creatures are instead surprised by you.</p>\n<p>Also, you no longer abandon the scrutinize approach if you can no longer see the designated target or area (unless you choose to).</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/investigation#toc17\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
